title: 'cpanfile: IO::Async::SSL missing although every built-in provider endpoint
  is https'
updated: 2026-10-15T04:48:06Z
---

All default endpoints are https (`Provider/Exa.pm:17`, `Google.pm:20`, `DuckDuckGo.pm:16`, `Mojeek.pm:20`, `Tavily.pm:17`, `Reddit.pm:16`, ...). Net::Async::HTTP needs IO::Async::SSL for https and loads it only while connecting; it does not depend on it itself (its META lists no SSL module). `cpanfile` here declares neither `IO::Async::SSL` nor `IO::Socket::SSL`, so on a clean install every provider fails at connect time.

Also undeclared, same-distribution and therefore harmless: `HTTP::Request` (used directly in `Provider/Serper.pm:11`, `Exa.pm:11`, `Tavily.pm:11`) and `HTTP::Response` in tests - only `HTTP::Request::Common` is listed.

Done when: `requires 'IO::Async::SSL', '0.12'` (and `HTTP::Request`) are in `cpanfile`.

